44
00:04:13,691 --> 00:04:14,172
[SPEAKER_00]: The whole book

45
00:04:15,426 --> 00:04:27,392
[SPEAKER_00]: That first one is like this... well, second one, describes the right level in so many different ways, to recognize, okay, that's... it's not like you're saying no to everything until you're tightly wound, that it's just you're going to burst.

46
00:04:27,992 --> 00:04:29,973
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's saying no to things you need to say no to.

47
00:04:31,034 --> 00:04:39,558
[SPEAKER_00]: Lust, aversion, distraction, delusion, irritation, choice, things that are based on your choice, that you actively maintain and do.

48
00:04:40,278 --> 00:04:44,040
[SPEAKER_00]: Weaknesses that you actively, in full awareness, give into.

49
00:04:45,737 --> 00:04:52,543
[SPEAKER_00]: And now, you don't just mindless, like, like, blindly just, okay, I'll just say no to this and keep the precepts and when, when is it happening?

50
00:04:53,363 --> 00:04:53,524
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

51
00:04:53,704 --> 00:05:00,449
[SPEAKER_00]: The point of keeping the precepts is so that your mind comes up with that feedback that's going to be almost certainly unpleasant initially.

52
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:03,071
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you don't try to get rid of that.

53
00:05:04,332 --> 00:05:05,834
[SPEAKER_00]: You can get rid of other stuff if you want.

54
00:05:07,245 --> 00:05:17,855
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's a bit more nuanced than just keep the precepts and bury it like a donkey or something, and then everything will fall into place, which just becomes another method, which I always criticize.

55
00:05:17,956 --> 00:05:28,866
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even if the right thing people can take, taking that external method, I just stick to this mindlessly, without recognizing my responsibility, my choice, my influence, and my refusal to

56
00:05:29,856 --> 00:05:34,940
[SPEAKER_00]: To bear the state of mind on that subtler level where the doubt is, where anxiety is.

57
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:40,003
[SPEAKER_00]: As I was saying this morning, you don't need great pains and great torment to bring these things up.

58
00:05:40,163 --> 00:05:46,028
[SPEAKER_00]: Just say no to the essential desires that you want, acting out of anger, and stay with what's left.

59
00:05:47,729 --> 00:05:48,750
[SPEAKER_00]: Not too much, not too little.

60
00:05:48,970 --> 00:05:49,971
[SPEAKER_00]: It's going to come up on its own.

61
00:05:52,092 --> 00:05:53,353
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the training.

62
00:05:53,413 --> 00:05:56,055
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the uptaking... upholding of the virtue.

63
00:05:57,855 --> 00:06:06,580
[SPEAKER_00]: Not just sort of technically learning all the allowables and non-allowables, and then revolving around that, to protect you magically from these mental states.

64
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:06,740
