00:48:48,879 --> 00:48:51,581
[SPEAKER_04]: Then I feel what... how freedom may taste.

744
00:48:51,621 --> 00:48:54,222
[SPEAKER_04]: Because, actually, I don't have to do anything at that point.

745
00:48:54,383 --> 00:48:59,606
[SPEAKER_00]: And I don't know whether... Yeah, well, see, no, yeah, because you can then say, well, what if I stop worrying about other people's fields?

746
00:48:59,966 --> 00:49:01,447
[SPEAKER_00]: There will be nothing, then I'll be at peace.

747
00:49:02,548 --> 00:49:06,470
[SPEAKER_03]: But you should stop worrying about other people's fields only when you're fully enlightened and there is no more...

748
00:49:06,831 --> 00:49:12,674
[SPEAKER_03]: But, like, to a small extent, I mean, like... Again, to a small extent, you shouldn't stop worrying about possibility.

749
00:49:12,754 --> 00:49:12,935
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

750
00:49:13,635 --> 00:49:16,597
[SPEAKER_00]: But you should stop beating the animal if it's not going there because of that

751
00:49:19,763 --> 00:49:26,268
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the middle ground, you see, because I say, OK, no, let the animal people who mean, OK, so I can drop the worry.

752
00:49:26,329 --> 00:49:26,869
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no, no, no.

753
00:49:27,209 --> 00:49:27,810
[SPEAKER_00]: I didn't say that.

754
00:49:28,711 --> 00:49:29,071
[SPEAKER_00]: You won't.

755
00:49:29,111 --> 00:49:34,155
[SPEAKER_03]: You need to worry on the right level, but not choke the animal as a result of it.

756
00:49:38,299 --> 00:49:41,281
[SPEAKER_04]: I think this is just that there is expansion of the mind, so there is more freedom.

757
00:49:41,301 --> 00:49:42,142
[SPEAKER_03]: There will be.

758
00:49:42,162 --> 00:49:43,203
[SPEAKER_03]: There will be, yeah.

759
00:49:44,183 --> 00:49:45,865
[SPEAKER_03]: I mean, that's even how the simile goes.

760
00:49:47,618 --> 00:49:49,239
[SPEAKER_03]: The cows roam in other people's crop.

761
00:49:49,479 --> 00:49:53,801
[SPEAKER_03]: If he doesn't do it, he'll get punished, he'll get beaten, he'll get put in jail, he'll pay the price, the fine.

762
00:49:54,441 --> 00:49:58,784
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he's really worried, and constantly keeps them back, and hits them, and ropes them, and everything.

763
00:49:59,324 --> 00:50:02,986
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, he recognizes they're wandering less and less, and then, they stop wandering.

764
00:50:03,686 --> 00:50:05,787
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, they are just staying here, and then, he goes to sleep.

765
00:50:06,448 --> 00:50:08,949
[SPEAKER_03]: Wakes up, cows are still there, haven't left.

766
00:50:09,729 --> 00:50:10,229
[SPEAKER_03]: No problem.

767
00:50:10,870 --> 00:50:13,991
[SPEAKER_03]: Because he did work through rightly directed worry.

768
00:50:19,096 --> 00:50:24,560
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's, again, that won't be visible if somebody still has a view that, well, I must deal with this.

769
00:50:24,640 --> 00:50:25,661
[SPEAKER_00]: I must get rid of this worry.

770
00:50:25,701 --> 00:50:26,422
[SPEAKER_00]: I must get rid of this.

771
00:50:26,542 --> 00:50:27,503
[SPEAKER_00]: Not, not necessarily.

772
00:50:36,870 --> 00:50:40,833
[SPEAKER_02]: Maybe I can just... one more in this topic that I asked before.

773
00:50:41,294 --> 00:50:45,177
[SPEAKER_02]: What would be the difference between doubt hindrance and doubt feather?

774
00:50:47,141 --> 00:50:47,661
[SPEAKER_04]: Wise doubt.

775
00:50:47,901 --> 00:50:49,642
[SPEAKER_04]: Sorry to interrupt, but I was thinking.

776
00:50:49,882 --> 00:50:50,482
[SPEAKER_04]: Wise doubt.

777
00:50:50,702 --> 00:50:54,703
[SPEAKER_04]: Sometimes there is like a wise doubt.

778
00:50:54,943 --> 00:50:56,783
[SPEAKER_03]: A wise doubt.

779
00:50:57,963 --> 00:50:58,903
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, there wouldn't be a doubt.

780
00:50:59,524 --> 00:51:00,744
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't be a doubt in this sense.

781
00:51:00,804 --> 00:51:02,584
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't be constraining you one way or the other.

782
00:51:02,664 --> 00:51:03,584
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't be pressuring you.

783
00:51:03,604 --> 00:51:06,205
[SPEAKER_00]: It would be like wisely deflecting and questioning.

784
00:51:06,225 --> 00:51:07,365
[SPEAKER_03]: But...

785
00:51:07,405 --> 00:51:07,985
[SPEAKER_03]: So, what do you think?

786
00:51:08,886 --> 00:51:10,806
[SPEAKER_03]: What would you think, if I ask you?

787
00:51:10,826 --> 00:51:11,606
[SPEAKER_03]: What would be the difference?

788
00:51:11,706 --> 00:51:12,646
[SPEAKER_03]: Just whatever comes to mind.

789
00:51:19,562 --> 00:51:24,144
[SPEAKER_03]: Between the doubt... Say it's the same doubt.

790
00:51:24,224 --> 00:51:24,944
[SPEAKER_03]: One fetters you.

791
00:51:26,064 --> 00:51:27,285
[SPEAKER_03]: One person is fettered by that doubt.

792
00:51:27,805 --> 00:51:29,486
[SPEAKER_03]: Another one is just hindered, but not fettered.

793
00:51:31,046 --> 00:51:34,268
[SPEAKER_03]: I guess that then brings the question, what's the difference between hindrances and fetters?

794
00:51:35,148 --> 00:51:35,388
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

795
00:51:35,908 --> 00:51:36,829
[SPEAKER_02]: That's pretty much it.

796
00:51:37,509 --> 00:51:39,530
[SPEAKER_03]: So, which one do you think is more fundamental?

797
00:51:39,830 --> 00:51:40,230
[SPEAKER_03]: Fetters?

798
00:51:40,350 --> 00:51:42,231
[SPEAKER_03]: The fetters are more fundamental.

799
00:51:42,291 --> 00:51:42,891
[SPEAKER_03]: Exactly.

800
00:51:42,911 --> 00:51:43,111
[SPEAKER_03]: Not.

801
00:51:43,771 --> 00:51:43,971
[SPEAKER_03]: Not.

802
00:51:44,171 --> 00:51:44,752
[SPEAKER_03]: It's hindrances.

803
00:51:44,872 --> 00:51:45,352
[SPEAKER_02]: It's hindrances.

804
00:51:45,372 --> 00:51:45,612
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

805
00:51:46,722 --> 00:51:51,366
[SPEAKER_03]: Hindrances... fetters are the result of untamed hindrances.

806
00:51:52,848 --> 00:51:55,891
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why they would start falling off, the closer to arhantship you get.

807
00:51:56,651 --> 00:51:59,334
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why the arhant is the destroyer of the hindrances.

808
00:52:00,735 --> 00:52:09,904
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's this individual giving in to sensuality, ill-will, restlessness, worry, anxiety, doubt.

809
00:52:10,384 --> 00:52:12,006
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what feeds the fetters.

810
00:52:14,042 --> 00:52:17,723
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what provides fuel for them, and thus they fetter you in return.

811
00:52:19,383 --> 00:52:29,585
[SPEAKER_03]: So, really, the difference between fetters and the... like, say, the first three fetters that fall off in a sotāpanna, it's because he has already been training rightly in regard to the five hindrances.

812
00:52:30,745 --> 00:52:33,426
[SPEAKER_00]: He's not blindly, irrationally trying to get rid of them.

813
00:52:34,146 --> 00:52:35,686
[SPEAKER_00]: He's not psychologizing them.

814
00:52:35,907 --> 00:52:37,627
[SPEAKER_00]: He's not managing them.

815
00:52:37,667 --> 00:52:42,948
[SPEAKER_00]: He allowed them to arise on the right level, and learn how to see through them, through not acting out of them.

816
00:52:43,624 --> 00:52:47,165
[SPEAKER_00]: That's that sutta that I often quote, because when people think, oh, so it's just buried, just buried.

817
00:52:47,565 --> 00:52:49,426
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, no, the sutta is quite clear.

818
00:52:49,846 --> 00:52:52,447
[SPEAKER_00]: You have perceptions of sensuality present themselves.

819
00:52:52,567 --> 00:52:53,427
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not a hindrance.

820
00:52:54,567 --> 00:52:58,128
[SPEAKER_00]: Wrongly attending to it, picking it up, that's now a hindrance.

821
00:52:58,208 --> 00:52:59,128
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why it's a hindrance.

822
00:53:00,149 --> 00:53:02,249
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the Buddha, in the same sutta, describes how you free.

823
00:53:02,289 --> 00:53:06,331
[SPEAKER_00]: Not, oh, then he thinks about this, and does that, and he becomes from the right, he moves to the left.

824
00:53:06,971 --> 00:53:09,591
[SPEAKER_00]: No, he says, he stops attending to them wrongly.

825
00:53:10,032 --> 00:53:11,172
[SPEAKER_00]: While the thing remains

826
00:53:13,780 --> 00:53:15,461
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you train in regard to the hindrance.

827
00:53:16,481 --> 00:53:20,763
[SPEAKER_00]: You do that sufficiently, the extent of the fetters will diminish.

828
00:53:22,103 --> 00:53:31,487
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, say, you start taking the right medicine, not perfectly, but more and more accurately, and some of the coarser symptoms of your illness just disappear.

829
00:53:32,227 --> 00:53:32,707
[SPEAKER_00]: They're cured.

830
00:53:33,488 --> 00:53:34,068
[SPEAKER_00]: They fall off.

831
00:53:36,159 --> 00:53:45,346
[SPEAKER_02]: So, like, in that case, when there is still hindrance of doubt in sotāpanna, but there is no feather of doubt.

832
00:53:46,807 --> 00:53:47,248
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

833
00:53:47,288 --> 00:53:54,373
[SPEAKER_02]: But, for example, the next two feathers are... the fourth feather is caṇḍarāga.

834
00:53:54,934 --> 00:53:57,976
[SPEAKER_02]: So, this would be for anāgāmī.

835
00:53:58,456 --> 00:53:59,417
[SPEAKER_02]: He gets rid of that.

836
00:54:00,038 --> 00:54:04,841
[SPEAKER_02]: And... but there still would be the hindrance of sensual desire.

837
00:54:05,142 --> 00:54:05,442
[SPEAKER_03]: For whom?

838
00:54:05,957 --> 00:54:06,717
[SPEAKER_02]: For anāgāmī?

839
00:54:07,498 --> 00:54:07,718
[SPEAKER_03]: No.

840
00:54:08,218 --> 00:54:08,438
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

841
00:54:08,678 --> 00:54:08,818
[SPEAKER_03]: No.

842
00:54:09,699 --> 00:54:12,260
[SPEAKER_03]: Hindrance, chandarāga, sensuality, that's gone.

843
00:54:12,841 --> 00:54:14,001
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the fetter.

844
00:54:15,582 --> 00:54:17,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, sorry, you meant the hindrance of sensuality?

845
00:54:17,243 --> 00:54:18,023
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah, I suppose.

846
00:54:18,043 --> 00:54:18,503
[SPEAKER_00]: The hindrance.

847
00:54:18,744 --> 00:54:19,944
[SPEAKER_00]: The hindrance of sensuality?

848
00:54:20,064 --> 00:54:22,325
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, it would be there, but it won't be the central hindrance.

849
00:54:23,406 --> 00:54:30,069
[SPEAKER_00]: It would, for him, it would be exemplified through the craving for being and craving for non-being, what the suttas describe.

850
00:54:31,090 --> 00:54:35,052
[SPEAKER_00]: See, it's the extent of the hindrance that determines the size of the fetter.

851
00:54:36,557 --> 00:54:40,921
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the size of sexual desire and anger and ill-will, it's gone in an anāgāmī.

852
00:54:41,781 --> 00:54:53,070
[SPEAKER_00]: But that which used to be wrongly attended, that was resulting in sensuality and anger, is now the craving for non-being, craving for being.

853
00:54:54,691 --> 00:54:58,494
[SPEAKER_00]: And that still hinders him to the extent that he wrongly attends to it.

854
00:55:01,536 --> 00:55:04,278
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, if he stops doing that, then all the ten hindrances are gone.

855
00:55:06,595 --> 00:55:09,397
[SPEAKER_03]: Sorry, the ten fetters and all the five hindrances have been destroyed.

856
00:55:09,957 --> 00:55:25,986
[SPEAKER_02]: So, according to that, for a sotāpanna, this hindrance of doubt, and the feather of doubt, then he would, like, there would be certain things for puthujjana, for which sotāpanna wouldn't have any more doubt.

857
00:55:28,256 --> 00:55:29,777
[SPEAKER_02]: Is it not the case?

858
00:55:30,078 --> 00:55:42,047
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, if you're comparing them, as I said before, when you asked about difference between the pressures, it would be maybe correct in theory, if you put them side by side, but from your point of view, you can never see that way.

859
00:55:42,527 --> 00:55:47,091
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if you're not a sotāpanna, whatever you're doubtful, is your fetter as well.

860
00:55:48,252 --> 00:55:51,955
[SPEAKER_03]: Because you're not training your mind in regard to the phenomenon of doubt.

861
00:55:53,176 --> 00:55:57,399
[SPEAKER_03]: The more you train your mind in regard to the phenomenon of doubt, you'll be less and less doubtful.

862
00:55:59,273 --> 00:56:05,155
[SPEAKER_03]: And when you're satipaṭṭhāna, then, whatever's doubtful there, it won't be fettering, it will be hindering you.

863
00:56:05,495 --> 00:56:10,656
[SPEAKER_03]: But the practice of dealing with it was always the same, because what you're dealing with is not the fetters.

864
00:56:11,617 --> 00:56:13,957
[SPEAKER_03]: You're dealing with hindrances, whether you're kutujana or an arahant.

865
00:56:14,077 --> 00:56:15,858
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, arahant wouldn't, leading up to an arahant.

866
00:56:17,518 --> 00:56:20,399
[SPEAKER_03]: So, fetters are the extent of the symptoms.

867
00:56:21,119 --> 00:56:23,260
[SPEAKER_03]: So, they offer you a measure.

868
00:56:24,500 --> 00:56:30,104
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that's what I mean.

869
00:56:31,385 --> 00:56:36,008
[SPEAKER_00]: In a way, it doesn't matter to figure out the difference, because the work is the same.

870
00:56:36,488 --> 00:56:39,310
[SPEAKER_00]: And to actually figure out the difference, you just need to do that same work.

871
00:56:41,211 --> 00:56:42,572
[SPEAKER_03]: But it can be helpful, obviously.

872
00:56:43,705 --> 00:56:48,388
[SPEAKER_03]: ...to people with certain, maybe, affinities and characteristics and ways of thinking.

873
00:56:48,508 --> 00:56:50,789
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why the Buddha did talk about fetters.

874
00:56:50,809 --> 00:56:54,432
[SPEAKER_03]: Mind you, he talked about fetters because they were constantly asking him about rebirth and stuff.

875
00:56:54,912 --> 00:56:55,372
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, this...

876
00:56:55,653 --> 00:56:57,494
[SPEAKER_03]: He said, well, let me give you a general guideline.

877
00:56:57,574 --> 00:57:00,496
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if it's like these three symptoms are gone, it's about like this.

878
00:57:00,536 --> 00:57:03,498
[SPEAKER_03]: If these five symptoms, it's more like this.

879
00:57:03,518 --> 00:57:06,720
[SPEAKER_03]: He wasn't necessarily to like, oh, well, it's one fetter, two, three.

880
00:57:06,740 --> 00:57:09,361
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, I felt the third one fall off and stuff like that.

881
00:57:09,922 --> 00:57:11,583
[SPEAKER_03]: It's training in regard to the five

882
00:57:12,503 --> 00:57:15,744
[SPEAKER_03]: Those are the five ways your mind will try to get you.

883
00:57:16,184 --> 00:57:20,145
[SPEAKER_03]: Every worry, every suffering that you have, will boil down to one of the hindrances.

884
00:57:20,205 --> 00:57:20,645
[SPEAKER_03]: It has to.

885
00:57:20,725 --> 00:57:21,926
[SPEAKER_03]: There is nothing in between.

886
00:57:22,446 --> 00:57:27,587
[SPEAKER_03]: It's either going to be based on desire, ill-will, restlessness, anxiety, or doubt.

887
00:57:29,027 --> 00:57:30,688
[SPEAKER_03]: Or that laziness and distraction.

888
00:57:34,369 --> 00:57:38,810
[SPEAKER_03]: Those are the five ways it tries to, like, get you to act, trick you, trap you.

889
00:57:50,513 --> 00:57:55,275
[SPEAKER_04]: So, are there any reasons to pick either these as a guidelines or three defilements?

890
00:57:58,316 --> 00:58:01,817
[SPEAKER_03]: We both, different times, whatever inspires you to do the right effort on the right level.

891
00:58:07,219 --> 00:58:13,381
[SPEAKER_02]: Specifically about sloth and power porn and this kind of, one of these events with power, because

892
00:58:14,577 --> 00:58:21,220
[SPEAKER_02]: When it comes to restlessness, it's kind of more intuitive what to... how to endure that.

893
00:58:22,261 --> 00:58:25,262
[SPEAKER_02]: To not, for example, start doing things left and right.

894
00:58:25,723 --> 00:58:31,926
[SPEAKER_02]: When it comes to slot-and-talk work, it is more like, no, now I'm going to stand up and do things to not be...

895
00:58:32,426 --> 00:58:33,006
[SPEAKER_02]: Right, right, right.

896
00:58:33,306 --> 00:58:35,668
[SPEAKER_02]: But it's some sense of aversion for slot-and-talk work.

897
00:58:35,688 --> 00:58:35,948
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

898
00:58:37,428 --> 00:58:41,731
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, so if, again, it depends on the... it's not always going to be the same slot-and-talk work.

899
00:58:42,987 --> 00:58:48,751
[SPEAKER_03]: If it's just drowsy and it's just constantly... you're drifting away, then, yeah, get up, wake yourself up in that sense.

900
00:58:49,732 --> 00:58:55,417
[SPEAKER_03]: But it's more like... when that pressure to, like, lay down, sleep or not want to...

901
00:58:55,677 --> 00:58:59,099
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't wanna think about my intentions now.

902
00:59:00,280 --> 00:59:01,901
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the important one to recognize.

903
00:59:02,742 --> 00:59:04,704
[SPEAKER_00]: If, like, oh, I'm sleepy, well, go to sleep.

904
00:59:05,724 --> 00:59:06,465
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe you are tired.

905
00:59:07,820 --> 00:59:10,122
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you wake up and don't want to get up.

906
00:59:10,182 --> 00:59:11,403
[SPEAKER_00]: I want to continue laying down.

907
00:59:11,503 --> 00:59:12,804
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, now you know it's laziness.

908
00:59:13,724 --> 00:59:14,185
[SPEAKER_00]: Then get up.

909
00:59:16,326 --> 00:59:21,250
[SPEAKER_03]: If you don't want to think about things that are unpleasant related to practice, well, you recognize, well, okay.

910
00:59:22,390 --> 00:59:24,712
[SPEAKER_03]: That's clearly because I don't want to deal with it.

911
00:59:25,633 --> 00:59:28,135
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm lazy on that level where it matters.

912
00:59:28,615 --> 00:59:31,357
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't mean I shouldn't be lazy and go and start doing random projects.

913
00:59:33,113 --> 00:59:40,236
[SPEAKER_00]: But when it comes to not tolerating these unwholesome states that try to pressure you to accept them, act out of them, you're never lazy there.

914
00:59:40,376 --> 00:59:44,038
[SPEAKER_00]: There is never a rest there.

915
00:59:44,458 --> 00:59:51,681
[SPEAKER_00]: On that mental level, where your intentions, where your choices are, where the gate is, where you open and close the entrance to the secret.

916
00:59:52,361 --> 00:59:52,722
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't.

917
00:59:52,982 --> 00:59:53,622
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't afford it.

918
00:59:54,578 --> 00:59:59,501
[SPEAKER_00]: But as I said, initially, you might feel like, I have to watch this all the time, but as we described, actually, it's not.

919
00:59:59,541 --> 01:00:04,043
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, you have an intention, and you know that it's there, and you don't need to police it.

920
01:00:05,204 --> 01:00:07,745
[SPEAKER_03]: You don't need to chase the thoughts that come out of it or go in.

921
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:12,928
[SPEAKER_03]: You just need to not lose the sight that, when that time to choose comes.

922
01:00:13,808 --> 01:00:14,668
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the important one.

923
01:00:17,310 --> 01:00:18,511
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's actually quite effortless.

924
01:00:19,251 --> 01:00:20,131
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, there's that similar...

925
01:00:20,151 --> 01:00:21,172
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't remember where I read it.

926
01:00:22,756 --> 01:00:25,158
[SPEAKER_03]: I think it was in the circus, but I might have come up with it.

927
01:00:25,238 --> 01:00:25,798
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't really know.

928
01:00:25,879 --> 01:00:26,959
[SPEAKER_03]: It was the swing.

929
01:00:28,461 --> 01:00:29,521
[SPEAKER_03]: The children on a swing.

