1130
01:15:04,761 --> 01:15:11,105
[SPEAKER_00]: And he knows that even if he just accidentally touches them, he'll chop his head off, the king.

1131
01:15:11,886 --> 01:15:13,547
[SPEAKER_00]: So he's fully confined with this.

1132
01:15:13,767 --> 01:15:18,350
[SPEAKER_00]: And any direction of movement is going to be the end of him.

1133
01:15:19,969 --> 01:15:21,290
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's his job, basically.

1134
01:15:22,070 --> 01:15:31,056
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he says, yeah, there would be one confinement, and obviously corresponds as an example, but the confinement that the Buddha teaches freedom from, it's even greater than that.

1135
01:15:32,738 --> 01:15:38,621
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole freedom from Atavāda, that it's going to feel very confined, claustrophobic, closed.

1136
01:15:39,362 --> 01:15:43,805
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there is no outside movement, they wouldn't fall within the movement.

1137
01:15:44,320 --> 01:15:48,364
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no outside action or choice that wouldn't fall within the internal intention of action.

1138
01:15:48,404 --> 01:15:49,545
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there is no outside of it.

1139
01:15:50,085 --> 01:15:54,069
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, you can say to yourself, okay, there's no outside of it and still imply the outside.

1140
01:15:54,690 --> 01:16:04,979
[SPEAKER_00]: You truly train yourself within that confinement by not giving in to this management that I talk about or trying to get rid of it and look for the problem where it isn't.

1141
01:16:05,020 --> 01:16:09,644
[SPEAKER_00]: That will confine you, that will feel uncomfortable to the extent that you resist it.

1142
01:16:12,527 --> 01:16:25,732
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's usually why people, like, feels like too much to ask, if you tell them your meditation is, as I said, 99.99% is going to be rooted in wrong reasons, and be taking you away from the direction where you should be going.

1143
01:16:26,612 --> 01:16:36,436
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said, yes, there can always be an exception to a rule, where somebody does genuinely, because physically they're exhausted of this, and they just want to wind down, not do anything, and they don't do it for that reason.

1144
